  "body": "## What changed\n\nA Wire Contour of a meshed model now posts its circles and fillets as G2 / G3 arcs. Before, they were G01 chords.\n\n- New module `crates/motion/src/wire_edm/model_arcs.rs`. It reads the one closed model profile back as lines and arcs:\n  - An arc stands on at least 3 facet chords. Each vertex is within 1 um of the circle. Each chord is at least 5 um long.\n  - Each chord bows off its arc by no more than the model chord tolerance (`CHORD_CAP` 0.005 mm plus the model excess). A true polygon (an octagon) stays a polygon.\n  - A run within 1 um of its end chord is a line. A radius over 1000 mm or under 0.01 mm is a line.\n  - Split points on a chord (from the section or silhouette) are dropped first, the nearest one first.\n- New module `crates/motion/src/wire_edm/model_tangent.rs`. A fillet end that meets a straight side within 1e-4 rad is made tangent to it. This prevents pivot arcs of no length (G1 blocks of no length).\n- The chain goes to the analytic wire contour of #3937 (`wire_contour_arcs`): concentric kerf arcs, the same kerf and cover laws, the same refusals by name.\n- `wire_op::generate_wire` takes the model chord (`None` for a selected DXF chain). Only the vertical, untabbed, one-profile cut reads arcs. Skims, tabs, burnout, exit pick, taper and 4-axis keep the polygon path (#3216, #3941).\n- A profile with no fitted arc keeps the polygon cut byte for byte.\n- `wire_verify`: a vertical model cut with arc moves is judged under the model chord plus the 1 um fit (0.006 mm). The verdict line says \"kerf judged under the model's chord tolerance\". The arcs pass between the facet chords and the true circle.\n- `sim::verify::wire`: the undercut law of #3210 now runs only when the cut states a taper (`taper_chord && taper`).\n- There is no B-rep path: the STEP and SolidCraft imports mesh each body, and the document keeps no analytic edge. The decision file has the reason.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/3215-wire-model-arcs.md`.\n\n## Readings\n\n- A dia-8 hole meshed at 63 chords (die, start at the centre), generic ISO post:\n  - two half arcs `G3 ... I-3.835 J0.` about (0, 0), radius 3.835 (4 - 0.165 kerf);\n  - 2 straight blocks (lead in and lead out).\n- The 40 x 20 die opening with 2 mm corners at 3-degree facets (`opening()` fixture of `wire_post`):\n  - before: about 120 G1 chords;\n  - after: 4 arcs about (+-18, +-8), radius 1.835, and 7 straight blocks (4 sides, one side split by the seam, lead in and out).\n- The same posted program for the Sodick post (`G02` / `G03`).\n- Verdict line of the `wire_verify` die: \"kerf judged under the model's chord tolerance 0.0060 mm: the kerf enters the model's facets by at most 0.0007 mm\" (the 3-degree chord sagitta is 0.68 um).\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `camcraft-motion` lib, `wire_edm::model_arcs_tests` (11):\n  - `a_meshed_hole_is_read_back_as_one_circle_and_cut_as_true_arcs`\n  - `meshed_fillets_are_read_as_arcs_between_the_straight_sides`\n  - `collinear_vertices_on_a_side_do_not_break_the_read`\n  - `a_profile_with_no_arcs_is_not_read` (rectangle, octagon, no chord)\n  - `degenerate_runs_stay_lines` (2-chord fillet, radius 5000 mm, 0.5 um wobble)\n  - `a_vertex_off_the_circle_is_never_read_into_an_arc`\n  - `the_laws_judge_the_read_arcs_and_catch_a_2_um_mutation` (kerf law refuses a 2 um shift; cover law refuses the arcs as chords)\n  - `a_meshed_inside_fillet_tighter_than_the_offset_is_refused_by_name`\n  - `a_cluster_of_noise_vertices_is_never_read_as_a_tiny_circle`\n  - `split_points_beside_polygon_corners_are_never_read_as_tiny_arcs`\n  - `fillets_on_a_nanometre_lattice_meet_their_sides_tangent_with_no_pivot`\n- `camcraft-sim` lib: `verify::wire::arc_tests::arcs_read_from_facets_pass_under_the_model_chord_on_a_vertical_cut`\n- `camcraft-app` `wire_post` (new submodule `wire_post/model_arcs.rs`):\n  - `a_meshed_hole_posts_as_two_half_arcs_not_chords` (ISO and Sodick, I/J checked)\n  - `meshed_fillets_post_as_arcs_between_the_straight_sides` (ISO and Sodick)\n  - `the_wire_laws_judge_the_read_arcs_under_the_model_chord`\n  - `a_profile_with_no_arcs_keeps_its_polygon_cut`\n- `camcraft-app` `wire_verify`: `a_correct_die_and_a_correct_punch_pass_and_name_the_piece_they_free` now also asserts the chord line.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No shipped wire golden uses a model with circles or fillets. The wire goldens (`wire_slug_punch.nc` for wire-iso and Sodick, `wire_contour_punch_skims.nc`, `wire_contour_open_cutoff.nc`, the `.cl` goldens `wire_contour_die`, `wire_contour_punch`, `wire_taper_punch`, `wire_4axis_punch`, `wire_open_cutoff`) are sharp polygons, skims, open runs, tapers or 4-axis cuts. They stay byte for byte, and this pins \"a profile with no arcs does not change\". The example catalog has no wire case.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No physical wire EDM machine or control ran the output.\n- The EDM-T1/T2/T3 STEP files (MIT licence) are not used as fixtures. A third-party file needs its notice in the tree, and a STEP import makes a slow test. The tests build the meshed hole and fillets in code, at the importer's chord. A run of the EDM-T2 block through the app is not done here.\n- The G-EDM post is not pinned by a new test here (it already writes G2 / G3 for the DXF arcs of #3937).\n\n## Gate\n\nAll on the final head `a7a32e421c4eca96459da0015e720d71efc370a3` (each log starts with that SHA):\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 184 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled, wall 31.5 min (log `gates/3215-a7a32e421.log`). The plan includes the pinning suites, every wire and Sodick / G-EDM / Agie suite of the gate maps, and `example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive`, `example_catalog_edge_work` (all ok).\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: 6 steps, 0 failed (log `gates/3215-a7a32e421-light.log`).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Before the commit, the wire suites ran one by one (`wire_post`, `sodick_wire_post`, `g_edm_post`, `wire_contour`, `wire_verify`, `wire_verify_tol`, `wire_dxf_selection`, `wire_burnout`, `wire_tabs`, `wire_taper*`, `wire_sharp_corners`, `wire_readers`, `wire_stamp`, `feature_pick_wire`, `mcp_wire_contour`, `wire_4axis`, `wire_fans`, `sodick_wire_passes`, `sodick_alc400g`, `sodick_wire_dielectric`, `wire_iso_decimal`, `agie_native`, `wire_post_alias`, `wire_tool`, `edm_machine`, `solid_law_goldens`): all ok.\n\nP6: no targeted heavy step (only a P1 PR under the safety floor runs one).\n\nNote on file length: `crates/app/src/operation/wire_op.rs` was 506 lines on main and is 508 now (one parameter, one `allow`). The new logic is in its own motion modules.\n\nChangelog: Wire EDM: a Wire Contour of a meshed model posts its circles and fillets as true G2 / G3 arcs (read back from the facets within the model chord tolerance), not as G01 chords.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #3215\n",
